# Run artefacts, not source.
#
# Every run writes results/<utc timestamp>-<type>/ with k6.log, summary.json,
# meta.json and the applied Job manifest. These are the evidence a result is
# explained by, so they are deliberately not cleaned up by the runners - but they
# are per-run output and do not belong in git. Accepted numbers live in baselines/.
results/

# Per-run kustomize overlays, regenerated from k8s/base on every deploy.
k8s/.generated/

# Publish output for the application image.
#
# Ignored for a security reason as much as a hygiene one: the publish folder is where
# the application's own .env is written so the container can reach HashiCorp Vault, and
# that file contains a live Vault token. An untracked-but-not-ignored .build/ is one
# `git add -A` away from committing a credential.
.build/

# Local credentials for the runners.
#
# k6/.env holds the account password, the login URL and any IdP client secret that
# run-test.ps1, run-journey.ps1 and deploy-and-test.ps1 read. k6/.env.example is the
# committed template; the real file never is.
.env
*.env
!.env.example
results/